IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`

-- Schedule 6 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376): the activities and descriptors by which a claimant's
-- limited capability for work is assessed, with the points each descriptor scores, and regulation 39(3) to (5), which adds
-- the points up.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies a slice of line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit (see uc4-seat.l4).
--
-- HOW THIS MODULE IS BUILT. The schedule is a table; the converter wrote each activity as one row and each cell on one line.
-- The points cell of a row is the points of its descriptors written one after another with nothing between them
-- ("159960" is five descriptors, 1(a) to 1(e)). The split used here is the only one that gives, for a row with n
-- descriptors, n numbers that never rise from one descriptor to the next and end in 0 (the last descriptor of every
-- row is "None of the above applies" or "Neither of the above applies"). That reading is fork F-points in NOTES.md.
-- Each activity has its own type, so that a form can offer only that activity's descriptors.
--
-- THE FACTS A CLAIMANT STATES, per activity: the descriptors that apply to the claimant, and what the incapability arises
-- from (regulation 39(4)). Regulation 39(5) counts only the highest-scoring descriptor of each activity.

§ `Regulation 39(4) — what the incapability must arise from`

-- src:755 | (4) In assessing the extent of a claimant's capability to perform any activity listed in Schedule 6, it is a condition that the claimant's incapability to perform the activity arises—
-- src:756 | (a) in respect of any descriptor listed in Part 1 of Schedule 6, from a specific bodily disease or disablement;
-- src:757 | (b) in respect of any descriptor listed in Part 2 of Schedule 6, from a specific mental illness or disablement; or
-- src:758 | (c) in respect of any descriptor or descriptors listed in—
-- src:759 | (i) Part 1 of Schedule 6, as a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease or disablement, or
-- src:760 | (ii) Part 2 of Schedule 6, as a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific mental illness or disablement.
@ref reg 39(4) (src:755-760)
DECLARE `Cause of incapability under regulation 39(4)` IS ONE OF
    `a specific bodily disease or disablement`
    `a specific mental illness or disablement`
    `treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease or disablement`
    `treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific mental illness or disablement`

-- Limbs (a) and (c)(i): a descriptor of Part 1 counts only if the incapability arises from a specific bodily disease or
-- disablement, or as a direct result of treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease
-- or disablement.
@ref reg 39(4) (src:755-760)
GIVEN causes IS A LIST OF `Cause of incapability under regulation 39(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 39(4)(a) and (c)(i) — the incapability arises as paragraph (4) requires for a Part 1 descriptor` causes MEANS
    (elem `a specific bodily disease or disablement` causes)
    OR (elem `treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease or disablement` causes)

-- Limbs (b) and (c)(ii): the same for a descriptor of Part 2, from a specific mental illness or disablement, or as a
-- direct result of treatment for it.
@ref reg 39(4) (src:755-760)
GIVEN causes IS A LIST OF `Cause of incapability under regulation 39(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 39(4)(b) and (c)(ii) — the incapability arises as paragraph (4) requires for a Part 2 descriptor` causes MEANS
    (elem `a specific mental illness or disablement` causes)
    OR (elem `treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific mental illness or disablement` causes)

-- Regulation 39(5) is quoted once here; each activity's highest-points rule below cites it.
-- src:761 | (5) Where more than one descriptor specified for an activity applies to a claimant, only the descriptor with the highest score in respect of each activity which applies is to be counted.

§ `Schedule 6 — Assessment of whether a claimant has limited capability for work`

-- src:2722 | SCHEDULE 6 — Assessment of whether a claimant has limited capability for work

§§ `Part 1 — Physical disabilities`

-- Activity 1. The points cell is the digits "159960": 5 descriptors, so 15, 9, 9, 6, 0 (fork F-points in NOTES.md).
-- src:2723 | PART 1 — Physical Disabilities
-- src:2724 | | (1) Activity | (2) Descriptors | (3) Points |
-- src:2725 | 1. Mobilising unaided by another person with or without a walking stick, manual wheelchair or other aid if such aid is normally or could reasonably be worn or used.
-- src:2725 | 1(a) Cannot, unaided by another person, either:(i) mobilise more than 50 metres on level ground without stopping in order to avoid significant discomfort or exhaustion; or(ii) repeatedly mobilise 50 metres within a reasonable timescale because of significant discomfort or exhaustion.
-- src:2725 | (b) Cannot, unaided by another person, mount or descend two steps even with the support of a handrail.
-- src:2725 | (c) Cannot, unaided by another person, either:(i) mobilise more than 100 metres on level ground without stopping in order to avoid significant discomfort or exhaustion; or(ii) repeatedly mobilise 100 metres within a reasonable timescale because of significant discomfort or exhaustion.
-- src:2725 | (d) Cannot, unaided by another person, either:(i) mobilise more than 200 metres on level ground without stopping in order to avoid significant discomfort or exhaustion; or(ii) repeatedly mobilise 200 metres within a reasonable timescale because of significant discomfort or exhaustion.
-- src:2725 | (e) None of the above applies.
-- src:2725 | 159960
@ref Sch 6 Part 1 activity 1 (src:2723-2725)
DECLARE `Sch 6 activity 1 descriptor` IS ONE OF
    `Sch 6 descriptor 1(a)`
    `Sch 6 descriptor 1(b)`
    `Sch 6 descriptor 1(c)`
    `Sch 6 descriptor 1(d)`
    `Sch 6 descriptor 1(e)`

@ref Sch 6 Part 1 activity 1, column (3) (src:2723-2725)
GIVEN descriptor IS A `Sch 6 activity 1 descriptor`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 6 activity 1 — the points for a descriptor` descriptor MEANS
    CONSIDER descriptor
    WHEN `Sch 6 descriptor 1(a)` THEN 15
    WHEN `Sch 6 descriptor 1(b)` THEN 9
    WHEN `Sch 6 descriptor 1(c)` THEN 9
    WHEN `Sch 6 descriptor 1(d)` THEN 6
    WHEN `Sch 6 descriptor 1(e)` THEN 0

@ref reg 39(5) (src:761)
GIVEN descriptors IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 1 descriptor`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 39(5) — the highest points among the descriptors that apply for Sch 6 activity 1` descriptors MEANS
    IF null descriptors THEN 0 ELSE maximum (map `Sch 6 activity 1 — the points for a descriptor` descriptors)

