-- src:2740 | 14(a) Cannot cope with any change to the extent that day to day life cannot be managed.
-- src:2740 | (b) Cannot cope with minor planned change (such as a pre-arranged change to the routine time scheduled for a lunch break), to the extent that, overall, day to day life is made significantly more difficult.
-- src:2740 | (c) Cannot cope with minor unplanned change (such as the timing of an appointment on the day it is due to occur), to the extent that, overall, day to day life is made significantly more difficult.
-- src:2740 | (d) None of the above applies.
-- src:2740 | 15960
@ref Sch 6 Part 2 activity 14 (src:2740)
DECLARE `Sch 6 activity 14 descriptor` IS ONE OF
    `Sch 6 descriptor 14(a)`
    `Sch 6 descriptor 14(b)`
    `Sch 6 descriptor 14(c)`
    `Sch 6 descriptor 14(d)`

@ref Sch 6 Part 2 activity 14, column (3) (src:2740)
GIVEN descriptor IS A `Sch 6 activity 14 descriptor`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 6 activity 14 — the points for a descriptor` descriptor MEANS
    CONSIDER descriptor
    WHEN `Sch 6 descriptor 14(a)` THEN 15
    WHEN `Sch 6 descriptor 14(b)` THEN 9
    WHEN `Sch 6 descriptor 14(c)` THEN 6
    WHEN `Sch 6 descriptor 14(d)` THEN 0

@ref reg 39(5) (src:761)
GIVEN descriptors IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 14 descriptor`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 39(5) — the highest points among the descriptors that apply for Sch 6 activity 14` descriptors MEANS
    IF null descriptors THEN 0 ELSE maximum (map `Sch 6 activity 14 — the points for a descriptor` descriptors)

